{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Male.</b> And not female; when he says זָכָר further on — which is not needed — מָה תַּ\"ל? Male and not a tumtum and not an androginos." "<b>Without blemish.</b> With no blemish." "<b>To the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> He deals with bringing it to the courtyard. What does יַקְרִיב יַקְרִיב tell us? Even if a burnt-offering of Reuben became mixed with a burnt-offering of Simeon, each one is offered in the name of its owner; and likewise a burnt-offering mixed with unconsecrated animals — the unconsecrated ones are sold for the needs of burnt-offerings, and behold they are all burnt-offerings, and each one is offered in the name of its owner. One might say even if it became mixed with disqualified animals or with an animal of a different species — Scripture says ״יַקְרִיבֶנּוּ״ (Sifra)." "<b>He shall offer it.</b> This teaches that we compel him. One might say against his will — Scripture says ״לִרְצוֹנוֹ״. How so? We compel him until he says: I am willing (ibid.)." "<b>Before YHWH, and lay his hand.</b> There is no semikhah on a bama (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:37.782175053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}